ConvomailInvoiceReadSetting = Fill from the invoice
ConvomailInvoiceReadSettingDesc = Off by default. When on, the supplier invoice panel offers a "Fill from the invoice" button: clicked, it reads the e-invoice data attached to the email (Factur-X, ZUGFeRD or XRechnung inside a PDF, or a UBL or CII XML file) on this server and fills the number, dates and amounts for the user to check. Nothing is read until a user clicks and nothing leaves the server. The supplier is selected from the document only when its VAT number matches exactly one supplier in Dolibarr, with a warning when the email does not come from one of that supplier's addresses.
ConvomailInvoiceAiSetting = Read with AI
ConvomailInvoiceAiSettingDesc = Off by default; needs "Fill from the invoice" and Dolibarr's AI module. When a PDF has no e-invoice data, the panel offers "Read with AI": clicked, the text of the PDF's first pages (up to 20,000 characters) is sent to the AI service set up in the AI module, and its checked answer fills the fields for the user to review. Bank details (IBAN, BIC, account numbers), email addresses and phone numbers are removed from the text before it leaves the server; amounts, dates, the invoice number and VAT numbers are sent, since they are what the AI reads. If you turned on the AI module's own privacy redaction, it masks names, addresses and VAT numbers too and puts them back in the answer; on Dolibarr 24.0 it also hides amounts and the invoice number, so the AI then fills little (fixed in 25). The request uses the AI module's document parsing (its own model setting from Dolibarr 25), and goes to the AI request log if you turned that on. Each click is one request to that service; a reading is kept a week so reopening the panel does not repeat it. A scanned PDF has no text to read.
ConvomailInvoiceAiNeedsModule = Needs Dolibarr's AI module, which is not enabled.
